course: dictionary
lesson: 11228
title: Woollen and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Woollen is an adjective. It tells you what something is made of: a woollen jumper is a jumper made of wool. Look at the word after it, such as jumper or socks, and you will see what woollen is describing.
explain: Woollens is a noun for clothes made of wool, such as jumpers and scarves. The -s makes it mean more than one piece of clothing. Spelling depends on where you live: British English writes woollen with two l's, and American English writes woolen with one.
explain: Read the sentence around the word for clues. «Holes in wool clothes are made by clothes moth caterpillars, not the adult moths, which do not eat at all.» The next part says washing, airing and freezing woollens gets rid of them, so woollens are clothes you can wash, air and freeze.
fact: «Woollen» means made of wool, as in «a woollen jumper» or «woollen socks».
fact: «Woollens» means clothes made of wool, such as jumpers and scarves.
fact: Wool comes mainly from sheep, and also from goats and alpacas.
fact: Wool traps air, which helps keep you warm in winter.
fact: Clothes moth caterpillars eat wool, fur and feathers, but the adult moths do not eat at all.
exercise: «Her woollen gloves kept her hands warm in the snow.» What is made of wool in this sentence? | *The gloves | The snow | Her hands | The winter sky
exercise: In «a woollen jumper», is woollen a noun or an adjective? | *Adjective | Verb | Noun
exercise: Wool mostly comes from which animal? | *Sheep | Horses | Pigs | Cows
test: Which word means clothes made of wool, such as jumpers and scarves? | Moth | *Woollens | Sheep | Wool
test: In «Holes in wool clothes are made by clothes moth caterpillars», who makes the holes? | *The caterpillars | The sheep | The adult moths | The washing
exam: According to the text, what gets rid of moth caterpillars in woollens? | Eating them | Shouting at them | Painting the clothes | *Washing, airing or freezing
